Mathematical extraction based on ADAM by Matti Viikinkoski and collaborators, exact revision25810f767b9de349a356df520109f4705f87f7a7. The upstream README declares Creative Commons Attribution4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ . Attribution is retained in local numerical source. No complete upstream program, FITS reader, WCS library, FFT library, parser, or domain library is shipped. The local C++17 kernels specialize the selected constant-albedo scattering model and use the standard library; Python supplies the complete local optimization and data flow. A memory-only adaptation moves the source center-of-mass early return after its already-written frees; no numeric expression changes. Numerical results are conditional method estimates, not ground truth.

The bundled reduced Hertha observations are author-supplied scientific data. A separate explicit data redistribution license was not found in the supplied files; this uncertainty is disclosed, not replaced with a presumed CC license. Local research validation is documented. Permission for wider redistribution of those observations remains unresolved.
